Hmm. So, Dr. Hellman, what about your path? Yeah, so this could take a couple of days. So roughly in the eighth grade, I transitioned into homelessness. It was a conscious decision for me. And I spent my high school years as a homeless youth. And moving into homelessness was a short-term goal centered around well-being and safety. and, you know, spending most days in school trying to keep that hidden because I was really afraid to become involved in the system, you know, at that time.

