hope. And it doesn't have to be rooted in, I don't think there's either one of those stances, either being religious or being atheist, that influences the degree of hope that one has. I think it really is about how you make meaning in the world. And the extent to which you have the capacity, the joy of being able to imagine. And for some people, the capacity to imagine has been so squashed by others around them, by structures around them, that their hope may be much smaller,

